  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The initial pressure and volume of an ideal gas are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. The final pressure of the gas when the gas is suddenly compressed to volume<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> will be:</p><p>(Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math>= ratio of specific heats at constant pressure and at constant volume.)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
